// A lemma about utf8.spec's definition `points`: a step of the proof, shown by the verifier before it is used
// (kbyte.py's prove_lemmas). It is not part of the specification and changes no meaning.
//
// `points` uses itself, from where the code point it has just read ends: at least one byte further, and not
// past the end. The count of bytes still ahead is less at each such use and never below zero: so it comes to an
// end on all bytes, with a count or failing.
lemma points(bytes: bytes, at: number, count: number): number {
    requires at <= len(bytes)
    decreases len(bytes) - at
}
